  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.6.0 — BREAKING to the documented exit-code contract, across the whole CLI. Usage errors now exit 64 (EX_USAGE) instead of 2, and — the actual defect — invocations that System.CommandLine answered before the handler ran no longer leak into the result band: a typo'd flag used to exit 1, which every audit gate documents as \"findings, build failed\", and --help exited 0, which for verify-archive means VERIFIED. The rule is now one sentence for every command: a result code is possible only when a handler produced it; everything else, --help and --version included, exits 64. Two crashes that printed stack traces are now one-line usage errors; an unexpected internal failure exits 70 and says so. If you script exit codes, read the \"Exit codes — NORMATIVE\" section of the CLI docs before upgrading.",
